From 100e80e8514d59febf8d412552c8ac9968f495ee Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Deniz Kokden <koekdendeniz@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:08:51 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 107/117] ARM: sprd: sc7730: modem core (CP) loader and SIPC

Port of the modem interface of the Samsung 3.10 kernel sources for the
SM-T561 (3G): sprd_cproc.c as arch/arm/mach-sprd/cproc.c and drivers/sipc
as arch/arm/mach-sprd/sipc/ (smsg message rings, smem pool, sbuf and sblock
data channels, spipe character devices, seth network devices). The tty
driver (stty.c) is left out, the stty_w devices come from spipe.

cproc keeps the userspace interface of the vendor driver (/proc/cpw/modem,
dsp, start, stop, status, wdtirq, mem), so the Spreadtrum userspace
(modem_control, phoneserver) can run unchanged. Ported to proc_ops,
wakeup sources instead of wakelocks, struct net_device and
platform_driver of 7.3, iomem pointers for the rings, and function
pointer tables with the types the callers use (kCFI).

The IPI register block needs its clock (AON_APB EB0 bit 21) before the
first SIPC access: without it the bus hangs. Samsung sets it in every
board init, here it goes with the counter clock in sc7730.c.

Device tree: sc7730-modem.dtsi (all nodes disabled, addresses from the
SM-T561 trees: CP memory 0x88000000, IPI 0x402c0000, IRAM1 0x50000000,
PMU 0x402b0000, smem 0x87800000), and sc7730-samsung-gtelwifi-modem.dts
that enables it on the SM-T560 for tests: that tablet has the same chip
and modem partitions, only no radio.

Tested on the SM-T560 in the rescue system: MODEM and WDSP written to
/proc/cpw, start: the core runs without a watchdog event, sends its
IPIs, all channels report ready, rmnet0-2 appear, and AT on stty_w0-15
answers OK; AT+CGMR returns the firmware version.

Assisted-by: Claude Sonnet 5.5
